# SECRETO · Boutique Erótica — environment template.
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in. Never commit real credentials.

# ─── Database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres connection string. Read by prisma.config.ts (CLI: migrate, studio,
# seed) and by src/lib/db.ts through the pg driver adapter (runtime).
#
# Leave it UNSET to run the storefront without a database: every catalog query
# falls back to src/features/catalog/fixtures.ts, which serves the same demo
# products. That is how the Phase 0 Vercel preview is deployed.
#
# Local:   postgresql://secreto:secreto@localhost:5432/secreto_dev?schema=public
# Managed: Neon or Supabase — append ?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/secreto_dev?schema=public"

# ─── Payments ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# "mock" until a merchant account is approved. PayU is the primary target,
# Wompi the second conversation — see docs/decisions/001-payment-provider.md.
# Never "stripe": prohibited category (CLAUDE.md).
PAYMENT_PROVIDER="mock"

# ─── Not wired yet ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Listed so the shape of the deployment is visible before Phase 3 needs them.
# Add the variable here in the same commit that first reads it.
#
# PAYU_MERCHANT_ID=
# PAYU_API_KEY=
# PAYU_API_LOGIN=
# PAYU_ACCOUNT_ID=
# Neutral descriptor on the buyer's statement — agreed with the gateway at
# onboarding, never the product or the legal name. "SECRETO BTQ".
# PAYMENT_STATEMENT_DESCRIPTOR="SECRETO BTQ"
#
# Cloudinary — product photography lives here, never in the repo.
# CLOUDINARY_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
#
# Transactional email. Sender name and subject stay neutral: no product names,
# no images, nothing that identifies the category in a notification preview.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM="SECRETO <pedidos@example.com>"
#
# Admin panel authentication (better-auth).
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
